            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0632" n="518" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg518"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A 4e 1/63: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-05-01T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1, 1924—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>84. With reference to the Department’s 80, April 24, 4 p.m., the Embassy at
                    London has reported<anchor n="36" xml:id="d506-f1"/> that the Foreign Office has
                    telegraphed the British Minister at Peking that he is to regard as definite
                    instructions the views shared by the American and British Governments as to the
                    reply that should be returned to the Chinese request for a preliminary
                    conference, and to act with you in this connection.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d506-f1" n="36" xml:id="d506-f1-content">
